  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who each route is for",
      "items": [
        "Admin: the internal LPS team. Signed-in admins can open every page and API path.",
        "Partner: a supplier with a portal login. Only /partner/... and /api/partner/..., and only their own company; other pages send them back to their portal, other API calls get \"forbidden\".",
        "Public: no sign-in. /login, /api/auth, the /public share links and published agent pages.",
        "Signed out on any other path: pages go to /login, API calls get \"unauthorized\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Worth knowing",
      "items": [
        "Admins can also open any /partner/[id] portal, to see what a supplier sees.",
        "An account on a generated password reaches only /change-password (plus /api/auth) until it picks its own.",
        "Static files (anything with a file extension, such as this handbook at /docs/*.html) skip the sign-in check.",
        "Old /portal/... links redirect to /partner/...."
      ]
    }
  ]
